{"id":"n-20261030-eiayrg","category":"tech","display_title":"AO3 Outage Security Incident","display_title_he":"תקרית אבטחה באתר AO3","short_summary":"The popular fanfiction archive AO3 could remain offline for up to four weeks following a security incident.","english_level":"C1","words":459,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d5/210830-H-DO456-101.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","credit":"CBP Photography · Public domain","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:210830-H-DO456-101.jpg"},"sources":[{"name":"TechCrunch","domain":"techcrunch.com","url":"https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/29/fan-fiction-site-archive-of-our-own-could-be-offline-for-up-to-4-weeks","title":"Fan-fiction site Archive of Our Own (AO3) could be offline for up to 4 weeks after security incident","published_at":"2026-10-29T20:43:56.000Z"},{"name":"IGN","domain":"ign.com","url":"https://www.ign.com/articles/archive-of-our-own-could-be-down-for-up-to-4-weeks-after-going-dark-for-emergency-maintenance","title":"Archive of Our Own Could Be Down for Up to 4 Weeks After Going Dark for Emergency Maintenance","published_at":"2026-10-29T20:01:56.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-29T20:01:56.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-30T07:48:45.005Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The popular fan-fiction website Archive of Our Own, widely known as AO3, faces an extended shutdown that could last up to a month following an unexpected security incident, according to platform administrators. What initially began as routine overnight maintenance quickly evolved into a major operational disruption for the dedicated reading community.","At 3:26 AM Eastern Time, the platform acknowledged it was offline for maintenance. Just a couple of hours later, representatives noted the work would require at least twelve hours. However, a later announcement revealed that service restoration would actually demand roughly two to four weeks, leaving loyal readers without their favorite storytelling destination for the foreseeable future. Within hours, status updates regarding the prolonged outage went viral on social media, picking up over seven million views and sparking widespread panic and panicked commentary among devoted users. Dismayed community members exploded into an apocalyptic frenzy, with one user calling it the worst tweet in history and others jokingly tagging official government accounts like the CIA, the FBI, and New York City Mayor Zohran Mamdani to demand immediate intervention.","Operated by the nonprofit Organization for Transformative Works, the platform relies heavily on volunteers and public donations to remain operational. Representatives stated that they are still in the early stages of investigating the scope of the incident. While administrators currently believe that the user database was not compromised, they admitted they cannot completely rule out a data breach. The platform's database stores account information including usernames, email addresses, IP addresses, and hashed passwords. Although passwords are protected using industry-standard hashing techniques, the organization strongly recommended that users update their credentials on any external services where they might use identical login information as a precautionary measure.","Addressing technical speculation, operators noted that the platform runs on the Ruby on Rails framework rather than PHP, distinguishing it from recent programming vulnerabilities affecting a large portion of the internet. While regular maintenance rarely causes shutdowns exceeding twenty-four hours, the service previously went down for three days this past March due to a database server issue. Earlier in the month, tools from OpenAI and Google Wiz uncovered two critical flaws in PHP, dubbed PHP Armageddon, leading to government demands for extra security, though this is unlikely to be connected to AO3's current situation.","Despite the severity of the outage, which affected a site hosting over eighteen million works, the Archive team expressed hope that they might restore a degraded, read-only version of the site sooner than the estimated two to four weeks. In the meantime, community members continue to share their dismay across social media platforms, while relying on locally downloaded files or archival tools like the Wayback Machine to access their favorite stories, though these alternatives prevent authors from receiving credit, comments, or Kudos."],"facts":[{"fact":"Archive of Our Own (AO3) went offline following a security incident and may remain down for up to four weeks.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"The site is operated by the nonprofit Organization for Transformative Works (OTW), relying on volunteers and donations.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Operators state that while user database theft is currently considered unlikely, it cannot be entirely ruled out.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The database contains account data such as usernames, email addresses, IP addresses, and hashed passwords.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Unlike many web services running on PHP, AO3 is built on the Ruby on Rails framework.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The platform hopes to restore a degraded or read-only version of the archive sooner than the full four-week estimate.","sources":[1,2]}],"glossary":[{"text":"popular","lemma":"popular","pos":"adjective","he":"פופולרי","name":false},{"text":"fan-fiction","lemma":"fan-fiction","pos":"noun","he":"ספרות מעריצים","name":false},{"text":"website","lemma":"website","pos":"noun","he":"אתר אינטרנט","name":false},{"text":"widely","lemma":"widely","pos":"adverb","he":"באופן נרחב","name":false},{"text":"known","lemma":"know","pos":"verb","he":"ידוע","name":false},{"text":"faces","lemma":"face","pos":"verb","he":"מתמודד עם","name":false},{"text":"extended","lemma":"extended","pos":"adjective","he":